# A certificate pair supplied by the deployment (SSL_CERT_FILE, SSL_KEY_FILE), imported by cms's
# Caddyfiles only when one is named (compose sets CADDY_SUPPLIED_PAIR). This site is here only to
# load the pair into Caddy's certificate cache, which every listener shares: a TLS handshake for a
# name the pair covers finds it there, and automatic HTTPS leaves those names alone ("skipping
# automatic certificate management" in the log). Every name the pair does not cover gets its
# certificate the usual way.
#
# No hostname, on a port compose does not publish: a site with a name the pair does not cover would
# have Caddy order a certificate for that name, and keep retrying. Standalone only: the full stack is
# HTTP only and imports nothing from docker/caddy/.
https://:4443 {
	tls /etc/caddy/tls/fullchain.pem /etc/caddy/tls/privkey.pem
	respond 404
}
